    {
      "section": "MCP Doctor for DSH",
      "text": "> Static validation of a local MCP JSON config. No server start, no handshake, no network."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\nnode bin/dsh-mcp-doctor.mjs ./mcp.json\nnode bin/dsh-mcp-doctor.mjs ./mcp.json --json\n```\n\nIn DSH:\n\n```text\nUse mcp_doctor on ./mcp.json.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Checks",
      "text": "- `mcpServers`, `mcp.servers`, or `servers` present\n- command/url present\n- command exists on PATH or absolute executable\n- URL syntax/protocol\n- args and env types\n- empty/duplicate names"
    },
    {
      "section": "Limits",
      "text": "- JSON only\n- Command lookup uses the current environment, not the MCP client's\n- No actual MCP handshake/tool enumeration/auth\n- Not a security audit"
    },
    {
      "section": "Tests",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm test\n```"
